WEBVTT

00:00:04.338 --> 00:00:07.341
I am Millia il Velch Cutrettola Turan.

00:00:07.592 --> 00:00:09.260
I am leading an operation
to take back our homeland

00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:12.013
as the royal representative
of the Turan Kingdom.

00:00:12.263 --> 00:00:16.184
I deeply apologize for the trouble
my people have caused you.

00:00:16.434 --> 00:00:19.896
I heard Turan fell.

00:00:20.146 --> 00:00:23.441
It hasn't fallen! I'm still here...!

00:00:23.691 --> 00:00:26.110
The kingdom's leadership
and army are no more.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:30.114
Can you really claim that Turan hasn't fallen?

00:00:30.364 --> 00:00:31.699
I realize what you're saying.

00:00:31.949 --> 00:00:34.368
That's why the Federation has to pay for--!

00:00:34.619 --> 00:00:36.996
I've no interest in your affairs.

00:00:37.246 --> 00:00:41.167
We've already made an agreement
with those Sky Pirates.

00:00:41.417 --> 00:00:43.044
An agreement?

00:00:44.212 --> 00:00:50.801
<i>No matter what might await us there</i>

00:00:51.052 --> 00:00:59.477
<i>I'll go to unexplored territory with you</i>

00:01:07.735 --> 00:01:15.785
<i>I just had a short dream</i>

00:01:16.035 --> 00:01:20.414
<i>In it, I saw your back</i>

00:01:20.665 --> 00:01:26.587
<i>Was it the past? The future?</i>

00:01:26.837 --> 00:01:37.348
<i>Ignore the needle on that meter
pointing to the red zone</i>

00:01:37.598 --> 00:01:40.476
<i>And go where the tailwinds
and your feelings point you</i>

00:01:40.726 --> 00:01:46.649
<i>Every time I flap my wings, it makes me realize</i>

00:01:46.899 --> 00:01:52.196
<i>That there are skies
I'll never be able to see again</i>

00:01:52.446 --> 00:01:57.702
<i>But if you still want to take flight</i>

00:01:57.952 --> 00:02:04.500
<i>Then I will be your wings</i>

00:02:27.315 --> 00:02:28.899
Princess Millia!

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:32.403
How could those girls be so stupid?!

00:02:32.653 --> 00:02:34.238
Where are they?!

00:02:35.281 --> 00:02:37.033
Princess Millia!

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:49.837
A single Vespa is all we have.

00:02:50.087 --> 00:02:52.923
Fifteen ships by ourselves might be rough...

00:02:53.966 --> 00:02:57.261
I'm countin' on you, Gisey!

00:03:01.974 --> 00:03:04.393
Sheesh! Fam!

00:03:04.643 --> 00:03:09.690
Is it me, or is the Silvius not
that different from our own ships?

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:14.487
Man, talk about roomy...

00:03:14.737 --> 00:03:18.115
These aren't like Vespas <i>or</i>
the Federation's Shaharzes...

00:03:18.366 --> 00:03:20.701
I wonder where these Vanships come from...

00:03:20.951 --> 00:03:22.620
--Seriously?!
--Awesome!

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:25.581
Oh! It's really Princess Millia!

00:03:25.831 --> 00:03:26.999
--It's her, in the flesh!
--Umm, uhh...

00:03:27.249 --> 00:03:29.335
--The white lily of Turan!
--Umm, uhh...

00:03:29.585 --> 00:03:31.504
Welcome, Princess Millia!

00:03:31.754 --> 00:03:33.798
How do you like being aboard the Silvius?

00:03:34.048 --> 00:03:36.342
Hey! You tryin' to beat me to the punch?!

00:03:36.592 --> 00:03:38.886
--You're the one standing there slack-jawed!
--Hey! Don't keep her standing! Get a chair!

00:03:39.136 --> 00:03:43.140
--| ain't slack-jawed!
--Listen, I'm looking for Fam...

00:03:43.391 --> 00:03:45.351
Not your chair! One for guests!
One that ain't busted!

00:03:45.601 --> 00:03:47.269
<i>Where is Pam?!</i>

00:03:47.520 --> 00:03:49.105
That's enough!

00:03:49.355 --> 00:03:51.482
What's going on here?!

00:03:56.320 --> 00:03:58.072
There she is...!

00:04:00.324 --> 00:04:02.368
Are you in charge here?

00:04:02.618 --> 00:04:04.495
--That's right.
--Fam!

00:04:04.745 --> 00:04:07.665
Explain yourself! What's this
about fifteen battleships?

00:04:07.915 --> 00:04:09.291
About that, actually...

00:04:09.542 --> 00:04:14.964
Think you could let me contact Kartoffel
so I can locate some Skyfish...?

00:04:15.214 --> 00:04:17.675
“Nwve?
"NQPe!

00:04:17.925 --> 00:04:19.885
--Cheapskate.
--Fam!

00:04:20.136 --> 00:04:22.179
Forget about making outside contact.

00:04:22.430 --> 00:04:24.557
How are we supposed to catch Sky-Fish, then?!

00:04:24.807 --> 00:04:25.683
One other thing.

00:04:25.933 --> 00:04:29.687
The captain says you're free to use
anything on board as you please.

00:04:29.937 --> 00:04:31.814
Baby Face thinks he's so high and mighty...

00:04:32.064 --> 00:04:33.607
Fan'!

00:04:33.858 --> 00:04:37.111
--Say what?!
--Oh, nothing...!

00:04:37.361 --> 00:04:39.113
First you make a deal without me,

00:04:39.363 --> 00:04:43.659
and now we're suddenly stealing
fifteen ships instead of just the Silvius...

00:04:43.909 --> 00:04:46.203
I guess I just couldn't help myself;

00:04:46.454 --> 00:04:51.417
it was like our ship-- err, Reaper--
had finally come in...

00:04:51.667 --> 00:04:53.169
Put it on!

00:04:56.172 --> 00:04:57.214
So cold...!

00:04:57.465 --> 00:04:59.633
Don't sound so disgraceful!

00:05:02.344 --> 00:05:04.013
Got it.

00:05:05.097 --> 00:05:08.559
--The Gyros constellation?
--Wow, you know your stuff, Princess!

00:05:08.809 --> 00:05:11.312
I know at least that much.

00:05:11.562 --> 00:05:13.856
Get ready, Fam...

00:05:14.106 --> 00:05:15.941
Now!

00:05:16.192 --> 00:05:17.735
Okay!

00:05:18.944 --> 00:05:23.115
Judging from the angle of elevation
and azimuth... One, two, three...

00:05:23.365 --> 00:05:26.410
We're 2.4 kilometers northwest
of the Kiirbis lookout,

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:30.706
moving south-southeast by east at 43 knots...

00:05:30.956 --> 00:05:35.002
We're pretty far west. The closest
Federation base would be...

00:05:35.252 --> 00:05:37.505
The Shahiya base is the only one for 100 miles.

00:05:37.755 --> 00:05:41.217
Making either the Ursragna
or the Aeshma our best target.

00:05:41.467 --> 00:05:43.636
What luck!

00:05:43.886 --> 00:05:46.263
We get two ships to choose from!

00:05:46.514 --> 00:05:49.183
How can you tell all that just
from our present position?

00:05:50.267 --> 00:05:54.772
Gisey has all the ships from the
past century stored in her head!

00:05:55.022 --> 00:05:57.066
--A whole century?!
--Yup!

00:05:57.316 --> 00:06:02.071
Even names, affiliations, captain
and key personnel profiles... Everything!

00:06:02.321 --> 00:06:03.697
I wouldn't say everything.

00:06:03.948 --> 00:06:05.991
I didn't know anything about
the Silvius, for example...

00:06:06.242 --> 00:06:08.244
Okay, so 90%!

00:06:08.494 --> 00:06:11.789
Hey! Can we use the
workplace below, Mister...

00:06:12.039 --> 00:06:15.084
...uhh, what was it again?

00:06:15.334 --> 00:06:17.795
I'm Olaf, Chief of Maintenance.

00:06:18.045 --> 00:06:19.630
All that from our current position?

00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:22.967
Yeah. These kids got some skill.

00:06:23.217 --> 00:06:26.303
Lend them assistance if they ask for help,

00:06:26.554 --> 00:06:27.846
as long as it doesn't affect your duties.

00:06:28.097 --> 00:06:30.307
Got it.

00:06:30.558 --> 00:06:32.518
Interesting kids, aren't they?

00:06:32.768 --> 00:06:34.895
I never would've imagined
you joining the Sky Pirates

00:06:35.145 --> 00:06:37.356
was why we lost contact with you...

00:06:39.567 --> 00:06:42.444
An Exile came down. I take it you know?

00:06:42.695 --> 00:06:43.696
Yeah.

00:06:43.946 --> 00:06:47.908
The key to the Exile that struck
Turan is Princess Liliana...

00:06:48.158 --> 00:06:50.119
...Millia's older sister.

00:06:51.328 --> 00:06:55.124
So the Federation used the Exile as a weapon?

00:06:56.375 --> 00:06:59.169
Princess Liliana was abducted and
taken to a Federation battleship,

00:06:59.420 --> 00:07:02.840
after which there was a Mysterion pulse.

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:09.430
Making peace with the Federation
will be difficult, in other words?

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:11.348
Probably.

00:07:17.938 --> 00:07:20.441
Check it out! This could work!

00:07:20.691 --> 00:07:23.569
Oh! Th-That's my collection...

00:07:24.987 --> 00:07:28.157
Could you possibly let us borrow them?

00:07:28.407 --> 00:07:30.367
Yeah...

00:07:30.618 --> 00:07:31.994
No fair, Elio!

00:07:32.244 --> 00:07:33.537
Don't forget us!

00:07:33.787 --> 00:07:37.291
We'll do anything you want, Princess!
Just give the word!

00:07:42.463 --> 00:07:48.010
Say, Fam. Why did you decide
to start hunting Skyfish for me?

00:07:48.260 --> 00:07:50.220
Why? Is it a problem?

00:07:50.471 --> 00:07:53.557
Oh, no.

00:07:53.807 --> 00:07:57.978
It's just that none of you
have any ties with Turan.

00:07:58.228 --> 00:08:01.982
Fam can't ignore people in need, that's all.

00:08:04.151 --> 00:08:09.073
But I can't give you anything in return.

00:08:09.323 --> 00:08:12.785
I don't have anything anymore...

00:08:17.331 --> 00:08:20.000
In that case, you can hold a Grand Race!

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:21.293
A Grand Race?

00:08:21.543 --> 00:08:26.006
Once you've taken Turan back,
let's make another Grand Race happen!

00:08:26.256 --> 00:08:29.093
Everyone'll fly through the peaceful skies again,

00:08:29.343 --> 00:08:32.930
and then I can prove my skill once and for all!

00:08:33.180 --> 00:08:35.557
Oh, Fam...

00:08:35.808 --> 00:08:39.019
Sounds like quite an expensive reward.

00:08:39.269 --> 00:08:41.438
<i>A well-deserved reward.</i>

00:08:47.403 --> 00:08:50.155
--All right, start her up.
--Okay!

00:08:54.785 --> 00:08:57.788
Hey! Short time, no see!

00:08:58.038 --> 00:09:02.084
--Dio?!
--Oh! The prodigal son returns!

00:09:03.711 --> 00:09:08.924
--You're with these people?
--Huh?! You're part of the Silvius crew?!

00:09:09.174 --> 00:09:11.093
Why didn't you tell us before?!

00:09:11.343 --> 00:09:14.430
--Oh, I never mentioned it?
--No!

00:09:14.680 --> 00:09:17.474
You could've given us more info, you know!

00:09:17.725 --> 00:09:18.892
We could've already--!

00:09:19.143 --> 00:09:20.602
Calm down, Fam!

00:09:20.853 --> 00:09:22.104
Anyway, have you heard?

00:09:22.354 --> 00:09:26.734
The Federation is going to formally
annex Turan in three days.

00:09:30.696 --> 00:09:32.573
Annex...?

00:09:41.248 --> 00:09:43.584
The kingdom's leadership
and army are no more.

00:09:43.834 --> 00:09:47.546
Can you really claim that Turan hasn't fallen?

00:09:53.260 --> 00:09:54.261
Where's Millia?

00:09:54.511 --> 00:09:57.556
The princess went to the lookout
deck to get some fresh air.

00:09:57.806 --> 00:09:59.600
Thanks!

00:10:11.236 --> 00:10:12.821
Millia.

00:10:13.071 --> 00:10:15.407
--Shouldn't you be getting ready?
--All finished.

00:10:15.657 --> 00:10:18.577
--Oh.
--Upsy-daisy...

00:10:20.621 --> 00:10:22.498
What nice wind!

00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:27.795
Millia...

00:10:29.922 --> 00:10:37.805
If Kartoffel ever disappeared, I'm sure
Giselle and I would be really sad.

00:10:38.055 --> 00:10:40.140
We love it so much...

00:10:40.390 --> 00:10:46.980
But if it ever happened,
we'd cry a lot, eat a lot, sleep a lot...

00:10:47.231 --> 00:10:52.778
...and then set out to create a new Kartoffel.

00:10:55.072 --> 00:11:00.244
Umm, I guess what I'm trying to say is...

00:11:00.494 --> 00:11:03.872
...as long as you're around,
Turan will never truly disappear.

00:11:06.333 --> 00:11:10.087
All you need is some territory
and people, you know?

00:11:10.337 --> 00:11:12.548
But I have no territory...

00:11:12.798 --> 00:11:16.176
It doesn't really matter <i>where</i> your territory is.

00:11:16.426 --> 00:11:18.637
Anywhere will do, even a house or a ship!

00:11:18.887 --> 00:11:20.806
Huh?

00:11:21.056 --> 00:11:24.142
People will flock to you
if you keep your spirits up!

00:11:24.393 --> 00:11:26.770
Okay! Look forward to the good news!

00:11:31.233 --> 00:11:33.110
Fam...

00:11:34.319 --> 00:11:37.114
Fuel, coolant, and Claudia are good to go.

00:11:37.364 --> 00:11:38.657
Fuel tank, check.

00:11:38.907 --> 00:11:42.578
Altimeter, gyro tuning,
and controls are all green.

00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:46.290
Pref light checks, all clear!

00:11:46.540 --> 00:11:51.086
--You gonna be okay?!
--Yes, it's almost exactly like a...

00:11:51.336 --> 00:11:52.379
...a Vespa...

00:11:52.629 --> 00:11:56.216
--Start 'er up!
--R-Right! Starting up!

00:12:00.679 --> 00:12:03.056
Fam! Fam!

00:12:03.307 --> 00:12:05.726
Are you sure you're going to be okay?!

00:12:05.976 --> 00:12:07.477
It's no sweat at all!

00:12:07.728 --> 00:12:11.273
We're gonna build an entire fleet for you!

00:12:11.523 --> 00:12:12.900
Y-You dummy!

00:12:13.150 --> 00:12:16.028
Mess up this time and you'll
have to answer to me!

00:12:19.698 --> 00:12:21.617
Okay, let's go!

00:12:41.094 --> 00:12:45.349
To establish a country, you need
a government, citizens, and territory.

00:12:45.599 --> 00:12:49.603
I'm the government,
and there's a citizen right here.

00:12:49.853 --> 00:12:51.229
Huh?

00:12:51.480 --> 00:12:52.940
R-Right!

00:12:53.190 --> 00:12:54.775
That just leaves territory!

00:12:55.025 --> 00:12:57.235
This ship's weakness is...!

00:13:00.322 --> 00:13:03.700
I have a request for Captain Tatiana...

00:13:03.951 --> 00:13:06.286
I never imagined you were
into playing dress-up...

00:13:06.536 --> 00:13:08.288
Looks pretty good on you.

00:13:08.538 --> 00:13:10.207
No, that isn't why I'm--

00:13:10.457 --> 00:13:12.626
You see, I have a citizen, and now I just need...

00:13:13.710 --> 00:13:18.590
Their defense is too strong! I can't
utilize this outfit's true power...!

00:13:18.840 --> 00:13:20.842
"Can't utilize... '

00:13:27.724 --> 00:13:29.059
Right on time.

00:13:29.309 --> 00:13:31.019
<i>Those are our targets'?</i>

00:13:31.269 --> 00:13:33.271
They look so lame with those spikes on 'em.

00:13:33.522 --> 00:13:34.898
They're from a time when a ship's strength

00:13:35.148 --> 00:13:37.150
was equated with its color
and its number of towers.

00:13:37.401 --> 00:13:41.113
How many towers does the
Ursragna have again? Two?

00:13:42.614 --> 00:13:44.074
Territory! Territory!

00:13:44.324 --> 00:13:47.452
There has to be a place
I can claim! There has to!

00:13:50.914 --> 00:13:53.917
Good food and sleep is all I look forward to!

00:13:54.167 --> 00:13:57.295
You can say that again! The food
here is what keeps me going!

00:13:57.546 --> 00:14:00.632
--Pops! Gimme seconds!
--Oh, me too!

00:14:04.636 --> 00:14:06.638
Here we go, Gisey!

00:14:06.888 --> 00:14:08.640
We'll seem suspicious if we run!

00:14:08.890 --> 00:14:09.933
Sheesh...

00:14:10.183 --> 00:14:13.854
Whoa, cool! She has three red towers!

00:14:15.689 --> 00:14:18.817
Narvik Command wants us to vacate the ship...?

00:14:19.067 --> 00:14:21.069
Yes. The Premier believes Shiraz,

00:14:21.319 --> 00:14:23.822
part of your captain's domain,
holds strategic importance.

00:14:24.072 --> 00:14:26.074
He is insistent on quelling
any possible rebellions.

00:14:26.324 --> 00:14:29.578
Shiraz? Never heard of it.

00:14:29.828 --> 00:14:31.955
Eep! That creepy pervert--!

00:14:32.205 --> 00:14:34.082
MY apfiflogies!

00:14:34.332 --> 00:14:39.421
This is the correct message for Lord Cirrus,
captain of the Prince of Victorius.

00:14:41.339 --> 00:14:43.633
It reads, "Lord Ernest Cirrus Lindemann...

00:14:43.884 --> 00:14:46.678
Your mother requests your immediate return."

00:14:46.928 --> 00:14:48.555
What?! My mother?!

00:14:48.805 --> 00:14:52.225
Yes. The letter gives strict orders
to arrive by tomorrow morning.

00:14:52.476 --> 00:14:58.607
Tomorrow morning?! There's no way!
Th-The Prince is too slow...!

00:14:58.857 --> 00:15:03.403
Yeah. This spiky Skyfish
would <i>never</i> make it in--

00:15:06.490 --> 00:15:10.619
Oh! Sir! A high-speed ship has been readied!

00:15:10.869 --> 00:15:13.413
What?! Ooh, excellent!

00:15:13.663 --> 00:15:16.750
Hang on, Mother! I'm coming!

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:18.627
Captain!

00:15:20.796 --> 00:15:23.423
So sorry...

00:15:23.673 --> 00:15:26.593
--Engine room under control!
--Bow turrets under control!

00:15:26.843 --> 00:15:30.972
--Aft lookout deck under control!
--Upper decks and all turrets under control!

00:15:34.601 --> 00:15:38.313
Can't believe we took over this big
of a ship without any fighting...

00:15:38.563 --> 00:15:41.566
Doing your homework and being prepared

00:15:41.817 --> 00:15:44.111
is 90% of any successful Sky-Fish hunt!

00:15:44.361 --> 00:15:47.948
All you need after that is guts
and bravery, not to mention beauty!

00:15:48.198 --> 00:15:49.699
You're really something...

00:15:49.950 --> 00:15:51.618
...Giselle!

00:15:57.666 --> 00:16:01.461
I would very much like your help!

00:16:03.964 --> 00:16:05.090
I beg of you!

00:16:05.340 --> 00:16:11.471
Turan is on the verge of destruction!
Please give me this room to save it!

00:16:15.475 --> 00:16:21.314
That's strange. I heard this kind of
outfit could touch any man's heart...

00:16:23.358 --> 00:16:25.068
"Ineffective..."

00:16:26.695 --> 00:16:30.574
Engine acoustics at <i>9</i> o'clock!
Ship-of-the-line class!

00:16:30.824 --> 00:16:34.452
All hands to battle stations.
Unknown ship-of-the-line approaching.

00:16:34.703 --> 00:16:37.455
Commence silent running. 15 to port.

00:16:37.706 --> 00:16:40.167
Silent running. 15 to port.

00:16:40.417 --> 00:16:42.335
Target ship's position?

00:16:42.586 --> 00:16:46.840
Present distance, 2.5. Closing in
at 80 knots calibrated airspeed.

00:16:47.090 --> 00:16:49.092
Observers. Request visual confirmation.

00:16:49.342 --> 00:16:51.845
All hands to battle stations. I repeat...

00:16:52.095 --> 00:16:54.514
5th Squad! Prepare for close quarters combat!

00:16:54.764 --> 00:16:56.308
Yes, Sir!

00:17:02.522 --> 00:17:03.481
Sir!

00:17:03.732 --> 00:17:05.567
Go on ahead!

00:17:05.817 --> 00:17:08.612
You better hide. This could be dangerous.

00:17:14.534 --> 00:17:16.620
P-Princess Millia...

00:17:24.753 --> 00:17:26.963
Acoustic signal from the approaching ship!

00:17:27.214 --> 00:17:30.759
"This is Olaf. Operation successful!"

00:17:31.009 --> 00:17:33.136
Took long enough...

00:17:33.386 --> 00:17:34.804
Stand down from battle stations.

00:17:35.055 --> 00:17:38.058
Approaching battleship has been
commandeered by the Sky Pirates.

00:17:38.308 --> 00:17:39.976
All right!

00:17:40.227 --> 00:17:43.063
It's Fam! She did it!

00:17:43.313 --> 00:17:45.023
Are you ready, Teddy?

00:17:53.782 --> 00:17:56.117
Huh? Time to eat already?

00:17:56.368 --> 00:18:00.247
I am the Second Princess
and royal deputy of Turan,

00:18:00.497 --> 00:18:03.458
Millia il Velch Cutrettola Turan.

00:18:03.708 --> 00:18:08.630
The Ades Federation has ignored our
sacred peace talks at the Grand Lake,

00:18:08.880 --> 00:18:11.633
mercilessly violated Turan's territory,

00:18:11.883 --> 00:18:15.178
and reduced our royal city to rubble.

00:18:15.428 --> 00:18:18.515
Not only that, it has expanded its invasion

00:18:18.765 --> 00:18:24.396
and now threatens neighboring
nations with its brutal onslaught.

00:18:24.646 --> 00:18:30.986
As a representative of the freedom-
and peace-loving Turan people,

00:18:31.236 --> 00:18:33.863
I resolutely vow to continue
fighting this Ades tyranny,

00:18:34.114 --> 00:18:38.451
and hereby establish the new
Turan Kingdom right here!

00:18:41.871 --> 00:18:43.748
The conquerors have been defeated,

00:18:43.999 --> 00:18:50.839
and the long-forgotten land of Gonia
has returned to its rightful owners.

00:18:51.089 --> 00:18:53.550
Fellow citizens who have
long suffered persecution!

00:18:53.800 --> 00:18:59.556
Unite now, more than ever,
and take back all that is yours!

00:19:01.141 --> 00:19:04.394
Gloria, Augusta!

00:19:16.656 --> 00:19:19.743
In the name of history and our forefathers,

00:19:19.993 --> 00:19:23.163
I hereby declare the annexation of Turan!

00:19:24.914 --> 00:19:30.337
A single planet, a single nation, a single people!

00:19:30.587 --> 00:19:32.589
May 9l°"Y be ours!

00:19:32.839 --> 00:19:34.299
Gloria, Augusta!

00:19:34.549 --> 00:19:39.637
Gloria, Augusta! Gloria, Augusta!

00:19:39.888 --> 00:19:45.810
Gloria, Augusta! Gloria, Augusta!...

00:19:51.024 --> 00:19:52.776
What are your demands?

00:19:53.026 --> 00:19:56.071
I want territorial rights over the kitchen,
shower room, and three private rooms

00:19:56.321 --> 00:20:02.202
for the Turan refugee government,
plus daily meals!

00:20:02.452 --> 00:20:04.788
Those are her demands.

00:20:06.664 --> 00:20:09.376
See? Interesting kids, huh?

00:20:11.127 --> 00:20:14.089
What shall we do?

00:20:14.339 --> 00:20:16.549
I suppose it's for a good cause...

00:20:16.800 --> 00:20:17.884
Are you sure?

00:20:18.134 --> 00:20:22.305
We could end up going head-to-head
with the Ades Federation, you know...

00:20:22.555 --> 00:20:26.267
You're the one who said making
peace with them would be difficult.

00:20:28.812 --> 00:20:33.024
You can't bear to leave
them in the lurch, can you?

00:20:36.277 --> 00:20:40.532
They seem pretty skilled for
a couple of lost birds, too.

00:20:45.495 --> 00:20:47.414
"CI-Coming through...
--Hey, don't push!

00:20:47.664 --> 00:20:49.833
--Princess Millia!
--What are you doing?!

00:20:50.083 --> 00:20:52.544
Whoa! What is this?!

00:20:52.794 --> 00:20:54.379
Is that you, Fam?

00:20:55.630 --> 00:20:57.590
You did it, Fam!

00:20:59.300 --> 00:21:01.344
What's with that outfit?!

00:21:02.387 --> 00:21:06.724
L-I had no choice! It's part
of the plan to rebuild Turan!

00:21:06.975 --> 00:21:09.811
--This is too much! My stomach hurts...
--You're laughing too much, Fam.

00:21:10.061 --> 00:21:12.147
"Fam finds it hilarious..."

00:21:14.399 --> 00:21:18.445
Congratulations on establishing
a refugee government!

00:21:20.530 --> 00:21:23.450
--This is from me.
--Thanks!

00:21:24.909 --> 00:21:27.078
Isn't this great?!

00:21:27.328 --> 00:21:30.165
What's wrong, Millia?

00:21:31.583 --> 00:21:33.918
I was just thinking how pathetic it is

00:21:34.169 --> 00:21:37.380
that this is the best I can do now...

00:21:39.174 --> 00:21:40.633
Millia...

00:21:40.884 --> 00:21:44.929
I don't know if I can really
rebuild Turan like this...

00:21:46.723 --> 00:21:52.228
But this is honest-to-goodness
territory you acquired all by yourself!

00:21:54.022 --> 00:21:57.609
This table is just the start!

00:21:59.194 --> 00:22:01.237
Soon you'll have all of the Silvius!

00:22:01.488 --> 00:22:04.324
And then it'll be time to take Turan back!

00:22:12.373 --> 00:22:17.962
There's no time to waste!
The Grand Race is waiting!

00:22:18.213 --> 00:22:19.797
Thank you.

00:22:30.892 --> 00:22:36.481
<i>How high are the skies,</i>

00:22:36.731 --> 00:22:42.529
<i>how strong are the winds,</i>

00:22:42.779 --> 00:22:48.368
<i>how clear are the waters</i>

00:22:48.618 --> 00:22:55.667
<i>you hold in your heart?</i>

00:22:56.876 --> 00:23:08.346
<i>One day I want to be the palm
of your hand and catch your tears</i>

00:23:08.596 --> 00:23:20.441
<i>I want us to share the
same sorrows, the same air</i>

00:23:20.692 --> 00:23:26.281
<i>I'll point the prow of this departing ship</i>

00:23:26.531 --> 00:23:35.081
<i>Right your way with no hesitation</i>

00:23:35.331 --> 00:23:41.045
<i>Let's raise the mast in this sea of wind</i>

00:23:41.296 --> 00:23:46.843
<i>And set sail on these waves of clouds</i>

00:23:47.093 --> 00:23:52.599
<i>With the faraway stars for a compass</i>

00:23:52.849 --> 00:24:00.523
<i>I'll head beyond the horizon with you</i>

00:24:03.443 --> 00:24:05.403
<i>Though it may seem like only one small step,</i>

00:24:05.653 --> 00:24:07.780
<i>it's a giant leap toward rebuilding Turan!</i>

00:24:08.031 --> 00:24:09.699
<i>The galley of the battleship Silvius...</i>

00:24:09.949 --> 00:24:12.160
<i>This is where our future begins!</i>

00:24:12.410 --> 00:24:14.537
<i>--Understand, Teddy?
--Yes, Princess Millia!</i>

00:24:14.787 --> 00:24:16.873
<i>Next is a room for Fam, Gisey, and myself.</i>

00:24:17.123 --> 00:24:19.709
Oh, Princess... What about me?

00:24:19.959 --> 00:24:21.586
<i>Oh!</i>

00:24:21.836 --> 00:24:26.799
<i>That's right! I'll need a room to
display my sister's keepsakes as well!</i>

00:24:27.050 --> 00:24:29.052
<i>What about</i> a <i>room for</i> me...?
